━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ StateMachines is facet of FunctionEmitter
    sees Calls
    sees LiveActions
    sees Loops
    sees MatchArms

_ starting-refined = false
_ stopping-object = false
_ immediate-passed LocalId = no-local

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-site Typed
    - id SyntaxId

` A state machine where it is written: the call of its function, given the environment in
` force here, which starts it and answers the value it starts in; one a property of a class
` holds, which a constructor starts, is given one of its own that holds the object (see
` `lone-environment`). The errors that leave its start leave the function with the call. One a
` line of a class's markup writes starts with those it refines (`start-content-machine`).
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. fact = call-at(id, .call-function)
. callee = if fact != no-fact then facts.calls[fact].callee else no-instance
if callee == no-instance || tables.instance-functions[callee] == no-function
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. written = facts.machine-of(callee)
if !starting-refined && written && written.store == .store-content && written.outer == 0
    = start-content-machine(id, written)
= call-machine(id, callee)

────────────────────
_ do start-content-machine Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - machine MachineFact

` Starts a machine written as a line of a class's markup, where the markup runs on the object:
` not for an object of a class whose markup writes a machine that refines it, which starts it
` instead (`refining-classes`); and where it refines another, the machines it refines start after
` it, as the reference starts the merged machine (`start-refined`).
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. skipped = tables.refining-classes(machine)
. done = ir.reserve-block()
if skipped.length != 0
    . running = ir.reserve-block()
    classes-branch(id, unit.self, skipped, done, running)
    ir.start-block(running)
do call-machine(id, machine.instance)
if machine.refined != no-instance
    starting-refined = true
    start-refined(facts.machine-of(machine.refined)!)
    starting-refined = false
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
= Typed(nothing, types.void-type)

────────────────────
_ do call-machine Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - callee InstanceId

` Calls a machine's function where it is written, given the environment in force here.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. lone = if unit.reading != unit.instance then lone-environment(id, no-slot) else no-local
. mark = pending.length
pending += if lone != no-local then load-local(lone, id) else written-environment(id)
. raising = instances.signatures[callee].errors.count != 0
takes-result = raising
. answer = call-instance(callee, id, mark)
takes-result = false
if raising
    answer = propagate(id, callee, answer.operand)
= Typed(answer.operand, instances.signatures[callee].returns)

────────────────────
_ do open-machine Bool
    - site SyntaxId
    - group U32 = U32.max

` Finds the machine the function being emitted is part of, or the one a group of event
` transitions is of, with what the binder declared for it. Says whether there is one.
. found = if group == U32.max then instance-machine else facts.machine-of-group(group)
    .. instance-machine = facts.machine-of(unit.instance) ?? facts.machine-of-group(group)
if !found
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    = false
machine-entering.clear()
= use-machine(found, site)

────────────────────
_ do use-machine Bool
    - found MachineFact
    - site SyntaxId

` Makes a machine the one emitted: what is kept of it, its parts and its cases, and the
` composite it is a piece of, where it is merged with others, with those of the machines that
` refine it (`below-pieces`). Says whether the binder declared what it keeps.
. row = bindings.machine-slots(found.module, found.syntax)
if !row
    refuse(.refused-function, site)
    = false
. items = tree.state-items(tree.state-body(found.syntax))
. cases = tree.machine-cases(items)
. composite = compose-machine(program, facts, found)
machining = Machining
    - found
    - row
    - items
    - cases
    - tree.machine-captures(items, cases)
    - composite
    - if composite then composite.piece-of(found.instance) else 0
    - if composite then below-pieces(found) else List'MachineComposite()
= true

────────────────────
_ do below-pieces [MachineComposite]
    - found MachineFact

` The composites of the machines that refine a machine, directly or through others.
. below [MachineComposite]
for fact in facts.machines
    if fact.outer != 0 || fact.refined == no-instance
        continue
    . current = facts.machine-of(fact.refined)
    while current && current.instance != found.instance
        current = facts.machine-of(current.refined) if current.refined != no-instance
    . composite = compose-machine(program, facts, fact) if current
    if composite
        below += composite
= below

────────────────────
_ do outer-machine MachineFact?
    - site SyntaxId

` The machine a named machine written in one of its cases is part of, or a refusal.
. found = facts.machine-at(machining.fact!.instance, machining.fact!.outer)
if !found
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
= found

────────────────────
_ do start-nested
    - item SyntaxId

` A named machine written in a case's body, started where the case's entry runs it, as the
` reference starts it: its first case is entered, its immediate transitions run, and the groups
` of its root are subscribed. The machine around it is emitted again after.
. found = facts.machine-at(machining.fact!.instance, tree.nested-machine(item))
if !found
    refuse(.refused-statement, item)
    =
. around = machining
if !use-machine(found, item)
    =
. initial = tree.initial-case(machining.items)
if initial != 0
    enter-case(initial, 0)
emit-immediates(machining.items, initial)
subscribe-groups(machining.items)
machining = around

────────────────────
_ do stop-nested
    - item SyntaxId

` A named machine written in a case's body, stopped where the case exits, as the reference
` stops it: the groups of its root are unsubscribed, then each of its active cases exits, and
` the tasks its cases' `TaskOwner`s still hold are cancelled. The machine around it is emitted
` again after.
. found = facts.machine-at(machining.fact!.instance, tree.nested-machine(item))
if !found
    refuse(.refused-statement, item)
    =
. around = machining
if !use-machine(found, item)
    =
unsubscribe-groups(machining.items)
exit-all()
sweep-tasks()
machining = around

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-start
    - declared SyntaxId

` A state machine's start, the body of its function, as the reference starts it where it is
` written: one a module's property is keeps its environment in the module's global for it,
` each case it projects is not active, it enters its first case and runs its
` immediate transitions, subscribes the groups of its root, and answers its value. One merged
` with others keeps its part for the object first (`keep-part`); one that refines another does
` only that, and the machine none refines starts after it, and subscribes the groups the pieces
` below it write at their roots after its own (`subscribe-roots`). Immediate transitions a
` machine that refines another writes at its root have no shape here.
if !open-machine(declared)
    =
if machining.composite
    keep-part(declared)
if tables.stops-at-close(machining.fact!)
    own-machine(declared)
if machining.fact!.refined != no-instance
    if tree.immediate-transitions(machining.items).length != 0
        refuse(.refused-statement, declared)
    return-nothing()
    =
if machining.fact!.store == .store-global
    . row = tables.storage-of(machining.fact!.module, instances.rows[unit.instance].decl)
    if row == no-storage || unit.environment == no-local
        refuse(.refused-statement, declared)
        =
    store-global(tables.storage[row], load-local(unit.environment, declared), declared)
for node in machining.cases
    project(node, false, make-operand(.operand-void, 0), declared)
. initial = tree.initial-case(machining.items)
if initial != 0
    enter-case(initial, 0)
emit-immediates(machining.items, initial)
subscribe-groups(machining.items)
subscribe-roots(declared)
. value = read-kept(machining.fact!.syntax, "(value)", declared)
return-value(value.operand, declared)

────────────────────
_ do subscribe-roots
    - site SyntaxId

` Subscribes the groups the pieces below the machine none refines write at their roots, in
` order, by the part of the one below it (`relay-part`).
if machining.composite && below-adds(U32.max, .part-subscribe)
    do call-below(U32.max, .part-subscribe, nowhere(), nowhere(), site)

────────────────────
_ do keep-part
    - site SyntaxId

` What a machine merged with others keeps for the object, where it starts: its environment, with
` its part (`emit-machine-part`), as a function value the object holds in the property named
` after its class, and, where it refines another, in the one that machine's part calls below it.
. name = part-name(machining.fact!)
. found = property-of(unit.owner-type, name) if name && unit.has-self
. held = if found then tables.layouts.objects[unit.owner-type] else no-layout
. code = tables.machine-part-of(unit.instance)
if !found || held == no-layout || code == no-function || unit.environment == no-local
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    =
. callback = make-callback(code, load-local(unit.environment, site), site)
. field = tables.layouts.field(held, object-header-fields + types.properties[found].slot)
store-struct(unit.self, field, callback, site)
. above MachineFact? = facts.machine-of(machining.fact!.refined) if machining.fact!.refined != no-instance
if !above
    =
. below = below-name(above)
. slot = property-of(unit.owner-type, below) if below
if !slot
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    =
store-struct
    - unit.self
    - tables.layouts.field(held, object-header-fields + types.properties[slot].slot)
    - callback
    - site

────────────────────
_ do own-machine
    - site SyntaxId

` Gives the event runtime, where a machine a class's property holds starts, what stops it, the
` function that does (`emit-machine-stop`) with the machine's environment, for the object's
` `close` to run (`event-stop-machines`).
. code = tables.machine-stop-of(unit.instance)
if code == no-function || unit.environment == no-local || !unit.has-self
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    =
. stop = make-callback(code, load-local(unit.environment, site), site)
. mark = pending.length
pending += num-cast(site, unit.self, managed-layout, pointer-layout)
pending += stop
do call-instance(facts.machine-own, site, mark)

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-stop

` The function that stops a machine a class's property holds, which the event runtime runs as
` the object closes, given the machine's environment, as a named machine written in a case stops
` where the case exits (`stop-nested`): the groups of its root are unsubscribed, with those the
` pieces below it write at their roots, then each of its active cases exits, and the tasks its
` cases' `TaskOwner`s still hold are cancelled (`sweep-tasks`), but for the task that runs the
` `close`, which the object keeps for its next `close` to cancel. A group of its root the class's
` table runs is left to it: the runtime closes the object's events next.
. machine = facts.machines[function.place]
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
returns-type = types.void-type
ir.returns = void-layout
if !open-machine(machine.syntax)
    =
unit = unit.received = true
. given = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
unit = unit.environment = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local(unit.environment, given, machine.syntax)
made-environment = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local(made-environment, load(given, 0, managed-layout, machine.syntax), machine.syntax)
share-self(machine.syntax)
unsubscribe-groups(machining.items, true)
if machining.composite && below-adds(U32.max, .part-unsubscribe)
    do call-below(U32.max, .part-unsubscribe, nowhere(), nowhere(), machine.syntax)
stopping-object = true
exit-all()
sweep-tasks()
stopping-object = false
return-value(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), machine.syntax)

────────────────────
+ do part-name Atom?
    - machine MachineFact

` The name of the property that holds what a machine merged with others keeps for the object:
` named after the class and the property whose machine it is.
= holder-name(machine, "part")

────────────────────
_ do below-name Atom?
    - machine MachineFact

` The name of the property that holds what the machine that refines a machine merged with others
` keeps for the object, which that machine's part calls (`call-below`).
= holder-name(machine, "below")

────────────────────
_ do holder-name Atom?
    - machine MachineFact
    - kind String

` The name of a property that holds a part for the object of a class whose property holds a
` machine merged with others, named after the class and the property, or whose markup writes
` one, named after the class and the machine's place among those of its markup.
. decls = program.modules[machine.module].decls
if machine.store == .store-content
    . unit-id = instances.rows[machine.instance].enclosing
    . type = if unit-id != no-instance then instances.rows[unit-id].self-type else no-type
    if type == no-type || !tables.is-class(type)
        = null
    . ref = class-ref(types, type)
    if ref.module != machine.module
        = null
    match? decls[ref.decl]
        | .decl-class(class)
            . position = program.modules[machine.module].tree.content-machines(class.content).find
                - machine.syntax
            if position != null
                = program.store-atom("(${class.name.text}-state-${position}-$kind)")
    = null
match? decls[machine.decl]
    | .decl-property(row)
        match? decls[row.owner]
            | .decl-class(class)
                if row.name
                    . property-name = row.name
                    = program.store-atom("(${class.name.text}-${property-name.text}-$kind)")
= null

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-part

` The part of a machine merged with others, the function the others call, as the reference runs
` the merged machine: given its environment, a case of the composite by its place, or its root
` for none, what to do (`PartOp`), and, where a joined group is tried, where the item and the
` broadcaster lie. A piece below calls it for a case it writes, or for the root of the machine
` none refines, to exit every active case; the piece above calls it for a case a piece above
` writes, or for the root, for what it and the pieces below it add there (`relay-part`). It
` answers whether an immediate transition or a joined group's transition passed, or a first case
` was entered.
. machine = facts.machines[function.place]
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
ir.add-argument(u32-layout)
ir.add-argument(u32-layout)
ir.add-argument(pointer-layout)
ir.add-argument(pointer-layout)
returns-type = types.bool-type
ir.returns = u8-layout
if !open-machine(machine.syntax)
    =
. composite = machining.composite
if !composite
    refuse(.refused-function, machine.syntax)
    =
unit = unit.received = true
. given = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
unit = unit.environment = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local(unit.environment, given, machine.syntax)
made-environment = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local(made-environment, load(given, 0, managed-layout, machine.syntax), machine.syntax)
share-self(machine.syntax)
. answer = ir.add-local(u8-layout)
store-local(answer, integer(.machine-u8, 0), machine.syntax)
. which = make-operand(.operand-argument, 1)
. op = make-operand(.operand-argument, 2)
. done = ir.reserve-block()
for case in 0 .. < composite.names.length
    . node = composite.node(case as U32, machining.piece)
    . owned = composite.owners[case] == machining.piece
    if owned && node == 0 || !owned && !relays-any(case as U32)
        continue
    . here = ir.reserve-block()
    . next = ir.reserve-block()
    branch
        - compare(machine.syntax, .compare-equal, which, integer(.machine-u32, case as U64))
        - here
        - next
    ir.start-block(here)
    if owned
        emit-owned-part(node, op, done)
    else
        relay-part(case as U32, op, answer, done)
    jump(done)
    ir.start-block(next)
if machining.piece == 0
    . exiting = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(is-part-op(machine.syntax, op, .part-exit-all), exiting, done)
    ir.start-block(exiting)
    exit-all()
else
    relay-part(U32.max, op, answer, done)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
return-value(load-local(answer, machine.syntax), machine.syntax)

────────────────────
_ do is-part-op Operand
    - site SyntaxId
    - op Operand
    - wanted PartOp

` Whether what a part is asked to do is one thing.
= compare(site, .compare-equal, op, integer(.machine-u32, wanted))

────────────────────
_ do part-branch
    - site SyntaxId
    - op Operand
    - wanted [PartOp]
    - matched IRBlockId
    - missed IRBlockId

` Leaves to `matched` where what a part is asked to do is one of those `wanted`, else to `missed`.
for position in 0 .. < wanted.length
    . next = if position + 1 == wanted.length then missed else ir.reserve-block()
    branch(is-part-op(site, op, wanted[position]), matched, next)
    if position + 1 < wanted.length
        ir.start-block(next)

────────────────────
_ do emit-owned-part
    - node SyntaxId
    - op Operand
    - done IRBlockId

` What a part does for a case it writes, where another piece calls it: keeps the case as entered,
` runs what it runs once entered and settles it or goes on to a case written in it, which the
` caller enters, or exits it where it is active, or exits the cases written in it. Only a case
` another piece can enter (`markable`) is entered so.
. leaving = ir.reserve-block()
if markable(machining.piece, node)
    enter-owned-part(node, op, done, leaving)
else
    jump(leaving)
ir.start-block(leaving)
. exiting = ir.reserve-block()
. below = ir.reserve-block()
branch(is-part-op(node, op, .part-exit), exiting, below)
ir.start-block(exiting)
exit-case-if-active(node)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(below)
. clearing = ir.reserve-block()
branch(is-part-op(node, op, .part-exit-below), clearing, done)
ir.start-block(clearing)
exit-descendants(node)

────────────────────
_ do enter-owned-part
    - node SyntaxId
    - op Operand
    - done IRBlockId
    - leaving IRBlockId

` What a part does to enter a case it writes, as `emit-owned-part` says, else leaving to `leaving`.
` One whose first case is given what its name is written with only where a path enters it
` (`enters-initial`) is never settled here.
. marking = ir.reserve-block()
. after-mark = ir.reserve-block()
. marks [PartOp]
marks += .part-enter
marks += .part-enter-step
marks += .part-mark
part-branch(node, op, marks, marking, after-mark)
ir.start-block(marking)
. turns = open-turns.length
machine-entering += node
enter-mark(node, 0)
machine-entering.pop()
close-turns(turns)
. marked = ir.reserve-block()
branch(is-part-op(node, op, .part-mark), done, marked)
ir.start-block(marked)
jump(after-mark)
ir.start-block(after-mark)
. entering = ir.reserve-block()
. entries [PartOp]
entries += .part-enter
entries += .part-enter-step
entries += .part-settle
entries += .part-step
part-branch(node, op, entries, entering, leaving)
ir.start-block(entering)
machine-entering += node
. entered = open-turns.length
enter-entry(node)
close-turns(entered)
. stepping = ir.reserve-block()
if tree.enters-initial(machining.items, node)
    . settling = ir.reserve-block()
    . settles [PartOp]
    settles += .part-enter
    settles += .part-settle
    part-branch(node, op, settles, settling, stepping)
    ir.start-block(settling)
    settle-case(node)
jump(stepping)
ir.start-block(stepping)
machine-entering.pop()
jump(done)

────────────────────
_ do relay-part
    - case U32
    - op Operand
    - answer LocalId
    - done IRBlockId

` What a part does, for a case a piece above writes or for the root for none, where the piece
` above calls it for what it and the pieces below it add there: what it adds (`relay-own`), then
` what the pieces below add, by the part of the one below it (`call-below`), except that the
` `do finally` blocks below run first and the cases below exit first. An immediate transition
` or a first case is tried below only where none here passes. A group joined with the group of
` a piece above is tried by this piece's handler, which tries those below; where this piece
` writes none, by the piece below.
. node = if case != U32.max then machining.composite!.node(case, machining.piece) else 0
. site = if node != 0 then node else machining.fact!.syntax
for wanted in relayed-ops()
    . own = relays(machining.composite!, machining.piece, case, wanted)
    . below = below-adds(case, wanted)
    if !own && !below
        continue
    . here = ir.reserve-block()
    . next = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(is-part-op(site, op, wanted), here, next)
    ir.start-block(here)
    . first = wanted == .part-finally || wanted == .part-exit-added
    . tried = wanted == .part-immediates || wanted == .part-initial
    if below && first
        do call-below(case, wanted, nowhere(), nowhere(), site)
    if own
        relay-own(case, node, wanted, answer)
    if below && !first && !(own && wanted == .part-initial)
        if own && tried
            . forwarding = ir.reserve-block()
            branch
                - compare(site, .compare-equal, load-local(answer, site), integer(.machine-u8, 0))
                - forwarding
                - done
            ir.start-block(forwarding)
        . passed = call-below(case, wanted, nowhere(), nowhere(), site)
        if tried
            store-local(answer, passed.operand, site)
    jump(done)
    ir.start-block(next)
if case == U32.max
    =
for piece in 0 .. < machining.piece
    . named = machining.composite!.node(case, piece)
    . source = program.modules[machining.composite!.pieces[piece].module].tree
    if named == 0
        continue
    for head in source.group-heads(source.state-items(source.state-body(named)))
        if source.is-state-handler(head) || other-first
            continue
        .. other-first = first-alike(machining.composite!, case, source, head) != piece
        . own = alike-in(machining.composite!, machining.piece, case, source, head)
        if own == 0 && !below-joins(case, source, head)
            continue
        . key = (PartOp.part-join as U64) + place-bits
            .. place-bits = group-place(machining.composite!.pieces[piece], head) as U64
        . here = ir.reserve-block()
        . next = ir.reserve-block()
        branch(compare(site, .compare-equal, op, integer(.machine-u32, key)), here, next)
        ir.start-block(here)
        if own != 0
            relay-join(own, group-place(machining.composite!.pieces[piece], head), answer)
        else
            . below = call-below
                - case
                - key as U32
                - make-operand(.operand-argument, 3)
                - make-operand(.operand-argument, 4)
                - site
            store-local(answer, below.operand, site)
        jump(done)
        ir.start-block(next)

────────────────────
_ do relays-any Bool
    - case U32

` Whether a part does anything, for a case a piece above writes, where the piece above calls it
` for what it and the pieces below it add (`relay-part`).
for wanted in relayed-ops()
    if relays(machining.composite!, machining.piece, case, wanted) || below-adds(case, wanted)
        = true
for piece in 0 .. < machining.piece
    . named = machining.composite!.node(case, piece)
    . source = program.modules[machining.composite!.pieces[piece].module].tree
    if named == 0
        continue
    for head in source.group-heads(source.state-items(source.state-body(named)))
        if source.is-state-handler(head)
            continue
        if alike-head || below-joins(case, source, head)
            = true
        .. alike-head = alike-in(machining.composite!, machining.piece, case, source, head) != 0
= false

────────────────────
_ do relay-own
    - case U32
    - node SyntaxId
    - wanted PartOp
    - answer LocalId

` What a part adds, for a case a piece above writes that it names again, or for the root for
` none, where the piece above calls it: runs the statements it adds to the case's entry, with the
` activations of the case and those above it it sees bound, once the `TaskOwner` it keeps for the
` tasks it spawns for the case is made, where it keeps one; keeps the case active here in a new
` generation and subscribes the groups it adds, or those it writes at the root; tries the
` immediate transitions it adds, answering whether one passed; unsubscribes those groups, the
` case no longer active here; runs the `do finally` blocks and stops the named machines it adds,
` last first, then cancels those tasks; exits the active cases it writes below the case, or
` anywhere, last first; or enters the first case it writes in the case, answering that one was.
` Immediate transitions it adds to a case where it adds a fallback have no shape here.
if wanted == .part-exit-added
    . cases = machining.composite!.descendants(case)
    . position = cases.length
    while position != 0
        position -= 1
        if machining.composite!.owners[cases[position]] == machining.piece
            exit-case-if-active(machining.composite!.node(cases[position], machining.piece))
    =
if case == U32.max
    subscribe-groups(machining.items)
    =
if wanted == .part-initial
    enter-case
        - machining.composite!.node
            - first-written(machining.composite!, machining.piece, case)
            - machining.piece
        - 0
    store-local(answer, integer(.machine-u8, 1), node)
    =
. items = tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node))
if wanted == .part-immediates && tree.immediate-fallback(items) != 0
    refuse(.refused-statement, node)
    =
. turns = open-turns.length
if wanted == .part-subscribe
    keep(node, "(active)", integer(.machine-u8, 1), node)
    . generation = read-kept(node, "(generation)", node)
    keep(node, "(generation)", add-one(generation.operand, node), node)
bind-path(node)
if wanted == .part-entries
    open-tasks(case-node(node), node)
    emit-entries(node)
else if wanted == .part-subscribe
    subscribe-groups(items)
else if wanted == .part-immediates
    immediate-passed = answer
    emit-immediates(items, node)
    immediate-passed = no-local
else if wanted == .part-unsubscribe
    unsubscribe-groups(items)
    keep(node, "(active)", integer(.machine-u8, 0), node)
else
    finish-items(items)
    close-tasks(case-node(node), node)
close-turns(turns)

────────────────────
_ do relay-join
    - head SyntaxId
    - joined U32
    - answer LocalId

` Tries a group a part writes that joins the group of a place among the facts' groups a piece
` above writes, by its handler, given the item and the broadcaster where the caller put them,
` and answers whether a transition passed. One whose item or stream is not that group's has no
` shape here.
. place = machine-group-of(head)
. handler = if place != U32.max then tables.machine-handler-of(place) else no-function
. given = facts.machine-groups[joined]
if handler == no-function || facts.machine-groups[place].item != given.item || other-stream
    refuse(.refused-statement, head)
    =
.. other-stream = facts.machine-groups[place].stream != given.stream
. mark = pending.length
pending += load-local(unit.environment, head)
pending += given-value(make-operand(.operand-argument, 3), given.item, head)
pending += given-value(make-operand(.operand-argument, 4), given.stream, head)
ir.depend(.callee-function, handler, may-panic-dependency)
store-local
    - answer
    - call
        - make-operand(.operand-symbol, tables.functions[handler].symbol)
        - head
        - mark
        - .callee-function
        - u8-layout
        - !in-landing
    - head

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-handler

` The function a group of a state machine's event transitions runs for an item, as the
` reference compiles it: given the machine's environment, the item and the broadcaster. Where
` the case that owns the group is not active it does nothing. Else `each` and `it` are the
` item, the activations of the owner and the cases above it are bound, and each transition is
` tried in turn, its pattern and
` its guard, and the first that passes fires; where none does, the group's fallback does. The
` machine's environment is the function's own, and the one it was given is that environment's
` link, from where the object the machine is written for is read, where it captures one. An
` error that leaves it is given to the global `unhandled-error`. A group of the root of a named
` machine written in a case of another does nothing where that case is not active. It answers
` whether a transition passed. Where the machine is a piece of a composite, the groups the
` pieces below join it with are tried after its own transitions (`try-joined`); one that joins a
` group a piece above writes has no fallback here.
. group = facts.machine-groups[function.place]
if !open-machine(group.head, function.place)
    =
. head = group.head
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.item, head))
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.stream, head))
returns-type = types.bool-type
ir.returns = u8-layout
unit = unit.received = true
unit = unit.environment = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local(unit.environment, make-operand(.operand-argument, 0), head)
made-environment = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local
    - made-environment
    - load(make-operand(.operand-argument, 0), 0, managed-layout, head)
    - head
share-self(head)
. item = make-operand(.operand-argument, 1)
. answer = ir.add-local(u8-layout)
store-local(answer, integer(.machine-u8, 0), head)
. done = ir.reserve-block()
if group.owner != 0
    . running = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(read-flag(group.owner, head).operand, running, done)
    ir.start-block(running)
else if machining.fact!.outer != 0
    . running = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(parent-flag(head), running, done)
    ir.start-block(running)
. each = bindings.declared-kind-at(binding-slots(), head, .slot-each)
. it = bindings.declared-kind-at(binding-slots(), head, .slot-it)
if each != no-slot
    bind-machine-local(each, item, group.item, head)
if it != no-slot
    bind-machine-local(it, item, group.item, head)
if group.owner != 0
    bind-path(group.owner)
if tree.is-state-handler(head)
    run-state-handler(head, group, item, done)
    ir.start-block(done)
    return-value(load-local(answer, head), head)
    =
. items = if group.owner != 0 then tree.state-items(tree.state-body(group.owner)) else machining.items
for transition in tree.group-transitions(items, head)
    . next = ir.reserve-block()
    . trigger = tree.state-trigger(transition)
    . pattern = tree.trigger-match(trigger)
    if pattern != 0
        do emit-pattern(pattern, Typed(item, group.item), next)
    . guard = tree.trigger-guard(trigger)
    if guard != 0
        . passed = ir.reserve-block()
        branch-on(guard, passed, next)
        ir.start-block(passed)
    fire-event(transition, group.owner)
    store-local(answer, integer(.machine-u8, 1), transition)
    jump(done)
    ir.start-block(next)
try-joined(head, group, item, answer, done)
. fallback = tree.group-fallback(items, head)
if fallback != 0 && joins-earlier(head)
    refuse(.refused-statement, fallback)
if fallback != 0
    fire-fallback(fallback)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
return-value(load-local(answer, head), head)

────────────────────
_ do run-state-handler
    - head SyntaxId
    - group MachineGroup
    - item Operand
    - done U32

` A handler's loop for an item of its stream, as the reference runs it: its pattern binds the
` item, or the item passes by where it fails; its `when` is tested; and its body runs.
match? tree.nodes[head]
    | .node-for-block(row)
        match? tree.nodes[row.loop]
            | .node-loop-syntax(loop)
                if loop.pattern != 0
                    do emit-pattern(loop.pattern, Typed(item, group.item), done)
                match? tree.nodes[loop.clause]
                    | .node-clause(clause)
                        . passed = ir.reserve-block()
                        branch-on(clause.expr, passed, done)
                        ir.start-block(passed)
                emit-statement(row.body)
jump(done)

────────────────────
_ do parent-flag Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` Whether the case of the machine around it that a named machine is written in is active.
. around = machining
. outer = outer-machine(site)
if !outer || !use-machine(outer, site)
    = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. flag = read-flag(around.fact!.parent, site)
machining = around
= flag.operand

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-cast

` The cast of a group's handler to the subscriber of its item, as the reference makes it: given
` the machine's environment, the item and the broadcaster, it runs the handler with them.
. group = facts.machine-groups[function.place]
. handler = tables.machine-handler-of(function.place)
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.item, group.head))
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.stream, group.head))
returns-type = types.void-type
ir.returns = void-layout
if handler == no-function
    refuse(.refused-function, group.head)
    =
. mark = pending.length
for position in 0u32 .. < 3
    pending += make-operand(.operand-argument, position)
ir.depend(.callee-function, handler, may-panic-dependency)
do call(handler-symbol, group.head, mark, .callee-function, u8-layout, !in-landing)
    .. handler-symbol = make-operand(.operand-symbol, tables.functions[handler].symbol)
return-nothing()

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-activation

` The function the subscriber a machine gives a broadcaster calls, as the reference makes it:
` given the record of the activation that subscribed, the item and the broadcaster, it runs the
` group's cast with the machine's environment the record holds, where the activation is still
` current, and answers that nothing went wrong. That of a group on an event of an object is
` what the port of the group runs, given the machine's environment itself, as the port runs it
` only while it is attached.
. group = facts.machine-groups[function.place]
. handler = tables.machine-handler-of(function.place)
. record = tables.machine-record
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.item, group.head))
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.stream, group.head))
returns-type = types.void-type
ir.returns = void-layout
. target = function-row(types, group.subscriber)
. carried = if carries(target) then facts.carried-result(target) else no-type
if carried != no-type
    return-results(carried, group.head)
if handler == no-function || record == no-layout
    refuse(.refused-function, group.head)
    =
. given = make-operand(.operand-argument, 0)
. running = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
. ported = group.event != U32.max
if ported
    jump(running)
else
    . active = load(given, tables.layouts.field(record, 1).offset, u8-layout, group.head)
    branch(compare(group.head, .compare-not-equal, active, integer(.machine-u8, 0)), running, done)
ir.start-block(running)
. mark = pending.length
pending += if ported then given else load(given, record-offset, managed-layout, group.head)
    .. record-offset = tables.layouts.field(record, 0).offset
pending += make-operand(.operand-argument, 1)
pending += make-operand(.operand-argument, 2)
. cast = handler + 1
ir.depend(.callee-function, cast, may-panic-dependency)
do call(cast-symbol, group.head, mark, .callee-function, void-layout, !in-landing)
    .. cast-symbol = make-operand(.operand-symbol, tables.functions[cast].symbol)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
return-value(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), group.head)

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-deferral

` The function the subscriber a machine gives a broadcaster that is no event calls, as the
` reference's `StateTransitionDeferral`: given the record of the activation that subscribed, the
` item and the broadcaster, it gives the event runtime's `event-machine-enqueue` the subscriber of
` the activation with them, which runs it once no event is being published and no other
` transition runs, and answers that nothing went wrong.
. group = facts.machine-groups[function.place]
. handler = tables.machine-handler-of(function.place)
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.item, group.head))
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.stream, group.head))
returns-type = types.void-type
ir.returns = void-layout
. target = function-row(types, group.subscriber)
. carried = if carries(target) then facts.carried-result(target) else no-type
if carried != no-type
    return-results(carried, group.head)
if handler == no-function || group.enqueue == no-instance
    refuse(.refused-function, group.head)
    =
. activation = make-callback(handler + 2, make-operand(.operand-argument, 0), group.head)
enqueue(group, activation, make-operand(.operand-argument, 1), make-operand(.operand-argument, 2))
return-value(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), group.head)

────────────────────
_ do enqueue
    - group MachineGroup
    - activation Operand
    - item Operand
    - broadcaster Operand

` Gives the event runtime's queue a group's activation, with an item and its broadcaster.
. mark = pending.length
pending += activation
pending += item
pending += broadcaster
do call-instance(group.enqueue, group.head, mark)

────────────────────
_ binding-slots RowRange'Slot

` The slots of the binding of the function being emitted.
RowRange'Slot(unit.slot-start, unit.slot-count)

────────────────────
_ case-node SyntaxId
    - node SyntaxId

` The node a machine keeps what it keeps for a case at: the case written, or what first names a
` case none writes.
if position != null then machining.cases[position] else node

.. position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(node)!)

────────────────────
+ do case-type TypeId
    - node SyntaxId

` What the case a node names holds in the machine's union.
. position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(node)!)
if position == null
    = no-type
match? types.rows[machining.fact!.union]
    | .type-named-union(row)
        = types.child-type(row.cases, position)
= no-type

────────────────────
+ do kept-slot SlotId
    - node SyntaxId
    - name String
    - site SyntaxId

` A slot the machine keeps under a name for a case, a group or itself, or a refusal.
. slot = bindings.machine-slot(machining.slots!, node, program.store-atom(name))
if slot == no-slot
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
= slot

────────────────────
+ do keep
    - node SyntaxId
    - name String
    - value Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` Stores what the machine keeps under a name in its environment.
. slot = kept-slot(node, name, site)
. held = find-captured(slot, site).type
keep-captured(slot, value, held, site)

────────────────────
+ do kept-type TypeId
    - node SyntaxId
    - name String
    - site SyntaxId

` The type of what the machine keeps under a name, as the type pass gave it.
. slot = kept-slot(node, name, site)
= find-captured(slot, site).type

────────────────────
_ do read-flag Typed
    - node SyntaxId
    - site SyntaxId

` Whether the case a node names is active.
. flag = read-kept(case-node(node), "(active)", site)
= Typed(flag.operand, types.bool-type)

────────────────────
_ do bind-machine-local
    - slot SlotId
    - value Operand
    - type TypeId
    - site SyntaxId

` Gives a name a part of a machine binds its cell, holding a value. One a nested function
` captures is kept in the environment of the turn of its activation, which the reference binds
` anew in each function that runs it; any other captured one has no shape here.
. offset = slot-offset(slot, site)
if is-captured(slot) && is-turned(slot)
    keep-captured(slot, value, type, site)
    =
if is-captured(slot)
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    =
. layout = layout-of(type, site)
if layout == void-layout
    =
. local = ir.add-local(layout)
rebindings += Rebinding(offset, unit.cells[offset])
unit.cells[offset] = local
store-local(local, value, site)

────────────────────
_ do restore-cells
    - mark Size

` Gives each cell a machine's name was bound to anew since `mark` the local it held before, last
` first, as the reference's scope of the activations an exit or an entry binds ends with it.
while rebindings.length > mark
    . restored = rebindings.pop()
    unit.cells[restored.offset] = restored.local

────────────────────
_ do bind-activation
    - node SyntaxId

` The names a case's or a continuation's activation sees, bound as the reference binds them,
` in a turn of the activation (`open-activation`): each name among what it gives to the part of
` what the case holds in its place, read from where the machine keeps it, and each name the case
` keeps to what it keeps.
. position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(node)!)
if position == null
    =
open-activation(node)
. held = case-node(node)
. targets = tree.state-targets(node)
. names [Atom]
if targets.count != 0
    . payload = read-kept(held, "(payload)", node)
    . whole = payload.type
    . layout = layout-of(whole, node)
    . offset = 0u32
    for target in tree.children[targets]
        match? tree.nodes[target]
            | .node-identifier(named)
                names += named.name
                . slot = bindings.declared-at(binding-slots(), node, named.name)
                if slot != no-slot
                    . piece = if targets.count == 1 then payload else part(payload.operand, layout, offset, target)
                    bind-machine-local(slot, piece.operand, piece.type, target)
        offset += 1
for name in machining.kept[position]
    if names.find(name) != null
        continue
    . slot = bindings.declared-at(binding-slots(), node, name)
    if slot != no-slot
        . kept = read-kept(held, "(kept ${name.text})", node)
        bind-machine-local(slot, kept.operand, kept.type, node)

────────────────────
_ do open-activation
    - node SyntaxId

` Starts a turn of the activation of a case or a continuation where its names are bound. One
` whose names nested functions capture has an environment of its own, as a loop's turn does: an
` object the collector owns, which arrives zeroed, linked to the environment in force around the
` activation (`turn-link`). Any other is noted as a turn with none, where a nested function
` written in it is given the one in force around it.
if unit.instance == no-instance
    =
. scope = tables.turn-scope(instances.rows[unit.instance].module, node)
if scope == no-scope
    . plain = activation-scope(node)
    if plain != no-scope
        open-turns += TurnScope(plain, no-local, no-place)
    =
. layout = tables.turn-environment(unit.instance, scope)
if unit.reading != unit.instance || stepping || layout == no-layout || layout == unbuilt-environment
    refuse(.refused-statement, node)
    =
. link = turn-link(scope, node)
. mark = pending.length
pending += integer(.machine-u64, tables.layouts.rows[layout].size)
pending += make-operand(.operand-descriptor, layout)
. made = call-runtime(.runtime-allocate-object, node, mark, managed-layout)
. local = ir.add-local(managed-layout)
store-local(local, made, node)
store(made, 0, link, true, node)
open-turns += TurnScope(scope, local, no-place)

────────────────────
_ do activation-scope ScopeId
    - node SyntaxId

` The scope of the activation of a case or a continuation in the binding of the function being
` emitted, or none.
. binding = instances.rows[unit.instance].binding
if binding == no-binding
    = no-scope
. range = bindings.bindings[binding].scopes
for scope in range.start .. < range.start + range.count
    if bindings.scopes[scope].syntax == node && bindings.scopes[scope].kind == .scope-activation
        = scope
= no-scope

────────────────────
_ do enter-case ?! Refused
    - node SyntaxId
    - via SyntaxId

` Enters a case, by the continuation `via` that led there where one did, and settles it.
. none [SyntaxId]
enter-below(node, via, none, 0, 0)

────────────────────
_ do enter-below
    - node SyntaxId
    - via SyntaxId
    - path [SyntaxId]
    - start Size
    - path-via SyntaxId

` Enters a case, as the reference expands its entry where a transition fires: it is kept as
` entered (`enter-mark`), by the continuation that led there where one did, whose entry
` statements then run and whose groups are subscribed, then what the case runs once entered
` (`enter-entry`). Then the cases of a path below it are entered from `start` on, the last by
` `path-via`, or where the path ends there, the case settles (`settle-case`). The turns of the
` activations it binds end there. A case entered again while its own entry is expanded has no
` shape here. One another piece of the machine's composite writes is entered by that piece
` (`enter-foreign`).
if machine-entering.find(node) != null
    refuse(.refused-statement, node)
    =
if foreign-case(node)
    enter-foreign(composite-case(node), via, start >= path.length, node)
    if start < path.length
        enter-path(path, start, path-via)
    =
machine-entering += node
. turns = open-turns.length
. rebound = rebindings.length
enter-mark(node, via)
if via != 0
    bind-activation(via)
    emit-entries(via)
    subscribe-groups(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(via)))
enter-entry(node)
if start < path.length
    enter-path(path, start, path-via)
else
    settle-case(node)
close-turns(turns)
restore-cells(rebound)
machine-entering.pop()

────────────────────
_ do enter-mark
    - node SyntaxId
    - via SyntaxId

` Keeps a case as entered, as the reference expands it where a transition fires: the case is
` active first, so that what a store of the machine's value runs finds it so, then the machine's
` value is made of what the case is given, by the continuation `via` that led there or else the
` case itself, and kept, with what the case holds and the names it keeps; the case is active in
` a new generation, with a `TaskOwner` where it keeps one (`open-tasks`), and projected so.
. activation = if via != 0 then via else node
. held = case-node(node)
. position = tree.case-position(machining.cases, tree.state-name(node)!)
if position == null
    refuse(.refused-statement, node)
    =
. holds = case-type(node) != types.void-type
. payload = make-payload(activation, case-type(node), position)
. value = make-union(activation, machining.fact!.union, position, payload)
keep-active(held, true, activation)
store-machine(value.operand, activation)
if holds
    keep(held, "(payload)", payload.operand, activation)
keep-names(held, activation, position)
. generation = read-kept(held, "(generation)", activation)
keep(held, "(generation)", add-one(generation.operand, activation), activation)
open-tasks(held, activation)
project(node, true, payload.operand, activation)

────────────────────
_ do open-tasks
    - node SyntaxId
    - site SyntaxId

` Makes the `TaskOwner` a case keeps for the tasks its activations spawn, the first time it is
` entered: each exit cancels what it holds then, so the next activation's tasks start alone.
` None is made where the program spawns none so.
if !keeps-tasks(node) || !makes-task-owners()
    =
. making = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
branch(present(site, read-kept(node, "(tasks)", site)).operand, done, making)
ir.start-block(making)
. made = call-instance(facts.task-owner-make, site, pending.length)
keep(node, "(tasks)", wrap(site, made, kept-type(node, "(tasks)", site)).operand, site)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)

────────────────────
_ do close-tasks
    - node SyntaxId
    - site SyntaxId

` Cancels the tasks the activation of a case owns as it exits, without waiting for them or
` yielding to them. A task that exits its own case, by sending what moves the machine, is not
` cancelled: the case's `TaskOwner` keeps it, for the case's next exit or the machine's stop to
` cancel (`sweep-tasks`). Where the object's `close` stops the machine, the task that runs the
` `close` is not cancelled either, and the object keeps it instead, as it keeps its own.
if !keeps-tasks(node) || !makes-task-owners()
    =
. mark = pending.length
pending += num-cast(site, read-kept(node, "(tasks)", site).operand, managed-layout, pointer-layout)
if stopping-object && unit.has-self && tables.is-class(unit.owner-type)
    pending += num-cast(site, unit.self, managed-layout, pointer-layout)
    call-runtime(.runtime-cancel-owned-tasks-to, site, mark)
else
    call-runtime(.runtime-cancel-owned-tasks, site, mark)

────────────────────
_ do sweep-tasks

` Cancels what each case's `TaskOwner` still holds as the machine stops: the tasks that exited
` their own case. A piece of a composite below the one that stops it keeps those of the cases it
` names again until their next exit.
for node in machining.cases
    close-tasks(node, machining.fact!.syntax)

────────────────────
_ keeps-tasks Bool
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether the machine keeps a `TaskOwner` for the activations of a case.
bindings.machine-slot(machining.slots!, node, program.store-atom("(tasks)")) != no-slot

────────────────────
_ makes-task-owners Bool

` Whether the program spawns a task a case's activation owns, for which it makes `TaskOwner`s.
facts.task-owner-make != no-instance && tables.instance-functions[facts.task-owner-make] != no-function

────────────────────
_ do enter-entry
    - node SyntaxId

` Runs what an entered case runs, as the reference expands it over the case's body merged with
` what the pieces below this one in the composite of the object's class add to it: the entry
` statements, with the activations of the case and those above it bound, then those the pieces
` add, then the case's groups are subscribed, then those the pieces add.
bind-path(node)
emit-entries(node)
contribute(node, .part-entries)
subscribe-groups(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node)))
contribute(node, .part-subscribe)

────────────────────
_ do settle-case
    - node SyntaxId

` Settles an entered case where no case below it is entered, as `emit-immediates` says.
emit-immediates(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node)), node, true)

────────────────────
_ do enter-foreign
    - case U32
    - via SyntaxId
    - settles Bool
    - site SyntaxId

` Enters a case of the machine's composite another piece writes, by that piece's part: kept as
` entered there, with the entry statements of the continuation `via` that led there, where one
` did, run here, then what the case runs once entered run there, and settled there where it
` `settles`. A case that holds what it is given, or keeps names, has no shape here, as its piece
` reads them where it enters it, nor has a continuation that subscribes groups, which its piece
` does not unsubscribe, nor one that spawns a task the case's activation owns, which its piece
` does not cancel, nor has one settled whose first case is given what its name is written with
` only where a path enters it.
. owner = machining.composite!.owners[case]
. items = if via != 0 then tree.state-items(tree.state-body(via)) else List'SyntaxId()
. written = machining.composite!.node(case, owner)
. fact = machining.composite!.pieces[owner]
. owner-tree = program.modules[fact.module].tree
. whole = owner-tree.state-items(owner-tree.state-body(fact.syntax))
. unsettled = settles && !owner-tree.enters-initial(whole, written)
. spawns = via != 0 && tree.spawns-in-body(via)
if !markable(owner, written) || tree.group-heads(items).length != 0 || unsettled || spawns
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    =
if via == 0
    do call-part(owner, case, if settles then .part-enter else PartOp.part-enter-step, site)
    =
do call-part(owner, case, .part-mark, site)
. turns = open-turns.length
. rebound = rebindings.length
bind-activation(via)
emit-entries(via)
close-turns(turns)
restore-cells(rebound)
do call-part(owner, case, if settles then .part-settle else PartOp.part-step, site)

────────────────────
_ markable Bool
    - piece U32
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether a piece of the machine's composite can keep a case it writes as entered for another
` piece, which gives it nothing: the case holds nothing it is given and keeps no names.
|? position == null || owner.state-targets(node).count != 0
    false
??
    owner.machine-captures(items, cases)[position].length == 0

.. owner = program.modules[machining.composite!.pieces[piece].module].tree
.. items = owner.state-items(owner.state-body(machining.composite!.pieces[piece].syntax))
.. cases = owner.machine-cases(items)
.. position = owner.case-position(cases, owner.state-name(node)!)

────────────────────
_ composite-case U32
    - node SyntaxId

` The case of the composite the machine emitted is a piece of that a node names, or none where it
` is no piece of one or no case of the composite has the name.
|? !composite || !name
    U32.max
??
    composite.case-named(name)

.. composite = machining.composite
.. name = tree.state-name(node)

────────────────────
_ foreign-case Bool
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether a node names a case of the machine's composite another piece writes, which only that
` piece keeps as entered or exits.
case != U32.max && machining.composite!.owners[case] != machining.piece

.. case = composite-case(node)

────────────────────
_ do contribute
    - node SyntaxId
    - op PartOp

` Runs what the pieces below this one in the composite of the object's class add to what `op`
` runs for a case this piece writes, where one adds anything (`relay-part`).
. case = composite-case(node)
if case != U32.max && below-adds(case, op)
    do call-below(case, op, nowhere(), nowhere(), node)

────────────────────
_ do piece-adds Bool
    - fact MachineFact
    - node SyntaxId
    - op PartOp

` Whether what a piece of a composite writes in the body of a case it names again adds anything
` to what `op` runs: entry statements, groups, immediate transitions or `do finally` blocks and
` named machines. A named machine also adds to subscribing and unsubscribing, where the piece
` keeps the case active for the groups of its root to read (`parent-flag`), and a `TaskOwner`
` the piece keeps for the case adds to entering and exiting it (`piece-keeps-tasks`).
. owner = program.modules[fact.module].tree
. items = owner.state-items(owner.state-body(node))
if op == .part-immediates
    = owner.immediate-transitions(items).length != 0
if (op == .part-entries || op == .part-finally) && piece-keeps-tasks(fact, node)
    = true
if (op == .part-subscribe || op == .part-unsubscribe) && owner.group-heads(items).length != 0
    = true
for item in items
    . nested = owner.nested-machine(item) != 0
    if (op == .part-subscribe || op == .part-unsubscribe) && nested
        = true
    if op == .part-entries && (nested || owner.is-entry-item(item))
        = true
    if op == .part-finally && (nested || owner.nodes[item] is .node-do-finally-block)
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do piece-keeps-tasks Bool
    - fact MachineFact
    - node SyntaxId

` Whether a piece of a composite keeps a `TaskOwner` for the activations of a case it names.
. owner = program.modules[fact.module].tree
. cases = owner.machine-cases(owner.state-items(owner.state-body(fact.syntax)))
. position = owner.case-position(cases, owner.state-name(node)!)
. row = bindings.machine-slots(fact.module, fact.syntax)
=? false if position == null || !row
= bindings.machine-slot(row, cases[position], program.store-atom("(tasks)")) != no-slot

────────────────────
_ do call-part Typed
    - piece U32
    - case U32
    - op PartOp
    - site SyntaxId

` Calls the part of a piece above this one in the machine's composite for a case, given what the
` object holds for that piece (`keep-part`).
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. code = tables.machine-part-of(machining.composite!.pieces[piece].instance)
. given = part-environment(piece, site)
if code == no-function
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. mark = pending.length
pending += given
pending += integer(.machine-u32, case)
pending += integer(.machine-u32, op)
pending += nowhere()
pending += nowhere()
. target = tables.functions[code]
ir.depend(.callee-function, code, if target.may-panic then may-panic-dependency else 0)
. called = call
    - make-operand(.operand-symbol, target.symbol)
    - site
    - mark
    - .callee-function
    - u8-layout
    - target.may-panic
= Typed(called, types.bool-type)

────────────────────
_ do call-below Typed
    - case U32
    - op U32
    - item Operand
    - stream Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` Calls the part of the piece below this one in the composite of the object's class, which the
` object holds in the property named after this piece's class (`keep-part`) where its class
` refines the machine, for a case or the root for none, given where a joined group's item and
` broadcaster lie, and answers what it answers, or false where there is none.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. name = below-name(machining.fact!)
. found = property-of(unit.owner-type, name) if name && unit.has-self
. held = if found then tables.layouts.objects[unit.owner-type] else no-layout
if !found || held == no-layout
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. field = tables.layouts.field(held, object-header-fields + types.properties[found].slot)
. answer = ir.add-local(u8-layout)
store-local(answer, integer(.machine-u8, 0), site)
. code = load(unit.self, field.offset, pointer-layout, site)
. calling = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(site, .compare-not-equal, code, integer(.machine-pointer, 0)), calling, done)
ir.start-block(calling)
. data = tables.layouts.field(tables.layouts.function-layout, 1).offset
. mark = pending.length
pending += load(unit.self, field.offset + data, managed-layout, site)
pending += integer(.machine-u32, case)
pending += integer(.machine-u32, op)
pending += item
pending += stream
store-local(answer, call(code, site, mark, .callee-value, u8-layout, !in-landing), site)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
= Typed(load-local(answer, site), types.bool-type)

────────────────────
+ nowhere Operand

` The address a part is given where it is given no item or broadcaster.
integer(.machine-pointer, 0)

────────────────────
_ do below-adds Bool
    - case U32
    - op PartOp

` Whether a piece below this one, in the composite of a machine that refines it, adds to what
` `op` runs for a case of this one's composite, or for its root for none (`relays`).
for composite in machining.below
    if relays(composite, (composite.pieces.length - 1) as U32, case, op)
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do below-joins Bool
    - case U32
    - source AST
    - head SyntaxId

` Whether a piece below this one, in the composite of a machine that refines it, writes a group
` in a case of this one's composite on the stream the group a transition of a piece above heads
` is on.
for composite in machining.below
    if alike-in(composite, (composite.pieces.length - 1) as U32, case, source, head) != 0
        = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do relays Bool
    - composite MachineComposite
    - piece U32
    - case U32
    - op PartOp

` Whether a piece of a composite adds to what `op` runs where the piece above it calls it for a
` case a piece above writes, or for the root for none: cases it writes below the case, or
` anywhere; the groups it writes at the root; the first case written in the case, where it
` writes it (`first-written`); or what it writes in the body of the case where it names it again
` (`piece-adds`).
. fact = composite.pieces[piece]
. owner = program.modules[fact.module].tree
if op == .part-exit-added
    for child in composite.descendants(case)
        if composite.owners[child] == piece
            = true
    = false
if case == U32.max
    = op == .part-subscribe && owner.group-heads(root-items).length != 0
        .. root-items = owner.state-items(owner.state-body(fact.syntax))
if op == .part-initial
    = first-written(composite, piece, case) != U32.max
. named = composite.node(case, piece)
= named != 0 && piece-adds(fact, named, op)

────────────────────
_ do first-written U32
    - composite MachineComposite
    - piece U32
    - case U32

` The first case of a composite written in a case, of those not entered by a trigger, where a
` piece of the composite writes it, or none.
for child in composite.children(case)
    . owner = composite.owners[child]
    if owner-tree.state-trigger(composite.node(child, owner)) == 0
        = if owner == piece then child else U32.max
    .. owner-tree = program.modules[composite.pieces[owner].module].tree
= U32.max

────────────────────
_ do alike-in SyntaxId
    - composite MachineComposite
    - piece U32
    - case U32
    - source AST
    - head SyntaxId

` The head of the group of event transitions a piece of a composite writes in a case, on the
` stream the group a transition of another tree heads is on, or none.
. named = composite.node(case, piece)
if named == 0
    = 0
. owner = program.modules[composite.pieces[piece].module].tree
for given in owner.group-heads(owner.state-items(owner.state-body(named)))
    if !owner.is-state-handler(given) && keyed-alike
        = given
    .. keyed-alike = source.alike-key(owner, source.state-trigger(head), owner.state-trigger(given))
= 0

────────────────────
_ do first-alike U32
    - composite MachineComposite
    - case U32
    - source AST
    - head SyntaxId

` The first piece of a composite that writes a group in a case on the stream the group a
` transition of a tree heads is on, or none.
for piece in 0 .. < composite.pieces.length
    if alike-in(composite, piece as U32, case, source, head) != 0
        = piece as U32
= U32.max

────────────────────
_ do part-environment Operand
    - piece U32
    - site SyntaxId

` The environment of a piece of the machine's composite, which the object holds with its part.
. name = part-name(machining.composite!.pieces[piece])
. found = property-of(unit.owner-type, name) if name && unit.has-self
. held = if found then tables.layouts.objects[unit.owner-type] else no-layout
if !found || held == no-layout
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. field = tables.layouts.field(held, object-header-fields + types.properties[found].slot)
. data = tables.layouts.field(tables.layouts.function-layout, 1).offset
= load(unit.self, field.offset + data, managed-layout, site)

────────────────────
_ do joins-earlier Bool
    - head SyntaxId

` Whether a group of event transitions joins the group a piece of the machine's composite before
` this one writes on the same stream in the case that owns it, as the reference joins the groups
` of a case's merged body: that piece's handler tries it (`try-joined`), and it is not subscribed.
. place = machine-group-of(head)
. owner = if place != U32.max then facts.machine-groups[place].owner else 0
if !machining.composite || owner == 0 || tree.is-state-handler(head)
    = false
. case = composite-case(owner)
if case == U32.max
    = false
for piece in 0 .. < machining.piece
    . named = machining.composite!.node(case, piece)
    . other = program.modules[machining.composite!.pieces[piece].module].tree
    if named != 0
        for given in other.group-heads(other.state-items(other.state-body(named)))
            if !other.is-state-handler(given)
                if tree.alike-key(other, tree.state-trigger(head), other.state-trigger(given))
                    = true
= false

────────────────────
_ do try-joined
    - head SyntaxId
    - group MachineGroup
    - item Operand
    - answer LocalId
    - done IRBlockId

` Where no transition of a group passed, tries the groups the pieces below this one in the
` composite of the object's class write on the same stream in the case that owns it, by the part
` of the one below it (`relay-part`), which is given where the item and the broadcaster lie and
` the place among the facts' groups of the group of the first piece that writes one there; one
` whose transition passes leaves to `done`.
if !machining.composite || group.owner == 0 || tree.is-state-handler(head)
    =
. case = composite-case(group.owner)
if case == U32.max
    =
. first = first-alike(machining.composite!, case, tree, head)
if first == U32.max || !below-joins(case, tree, head)
    =
. joined = alike-in(machining.composite!, first, case, tree, head)
. place = group-place(machining.composite!.pieces[first], joined)
if place == U32.max
    refuse(.refused-statement, head)
    =
. held = ir.add-local(layout-of(group.item, head), true)
. stream = ir.add-local(layout-of(group.stream, head), true)
store-local(held, item, head)
store-local(stream, make-operand(.operand-argument, 2), head)
. key = (PartOp.part-join as U64) + (place as U64)
. at = make-operand(.operand-value, append(.op-local-address, head, Span(), held, pointer-layout))
. from = make-operand
    - .operand-value
    - append(.op-local-address, head, Span(), stream, pointer-layout)
. passed = call-below(case, key as U32, at, from, head)
. passing = ir.reserve-block()
. next = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(head, .compare-not-equal, passed.operand, integer(.machine-u8, 0)), passing, next)
ir.start-block(passing)
store-local(answer, integer(.machine-u8, 1), head)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(next)

────────────────────
_ do group-place U32
    - machine MachineFact
    - head SyntaxId

` The place among the facts' groups of the group a transition of a machine heads, or none.
for position in machine.groups.start .. < machine.groups.start + machine.groups.count
    if facts.machine-groups[position].head == head
        = position
= U32.max

────────────────────
_ do enter-path ?! Refused
    - path [SyntaxId]
    - start Size
    - via SyntaxId

` Enters the cases of a path from a place on, each below the one before it, which does not
` settle; the last is entered by the continuation `via` where one leads there. Where the machine
` is a piece of a composite, the path is entered as the composite's (`enter-steps`).
. steps = composite-steps(path)
if steps.length != 0
    enter-steps(steps, start, via)
    =
if start + 1 < path.length
    enter-below(path[start], 0, path, start + 1, via)
else
    enter-case(path[start], via)

────────────────────
_ do enter-steps ?! Refused
    - steps [U32]
    - start Size
    - via SyntaxId

` Enters the cases of a path of the machine's composite from a place on, as `enter-path` does,
` where each case this piece does not write is entered by the piece that does (`enter-foreign`).
. case = steps[start]
. last = start + 1 == steps.length
. node = machining.composite!.node(case, machining.piece)
. site = if node != 0 then node else machining.fact!.syntax
if machining.composite!.owners[case] != machining.piece
    enter-foreign(case, if last then via else 0, last, if via != 0 then via else site)
    if !last
        enter-steps(steps, start + 1, via)
    =
if last
    enter-case(node, via)
    =
if machine-entering.find(node) != null
    refuse(.refused-statement, node)
    =
machine-entering += node
. turns = open-turns.length
enter-mark(node, 0)
enter-entry(node)
enter-steps(steps, start + 1, via)
close-turns(turns)
machine-entering.pop()

────────────────────
_ do composite-steps [U32]
    - path [SyntaxId]

` The cases of the machine's composite a path of this piece's cases names, or none where the
` machine is no piece of one or the path names a case none writes.
. steps [U32]
if !machining.composite
    = steps
for node in path
    . case = composite-case(node)
    if case == U32.max
        = List'U32()
    steps += case
= steps

────────────────────
_ composite-path [U32]
    - name Atom

` The cases from the root of the machine's composite down to the case of a name this piece does
` not write, the case last, or none.
|? !composite || tree.find-case(machining.items, name) != 0 || case == U32.max
    List'U32()
??
    composite.path-to(case)

.. composite = machining.composite
.. case = composite.case-named(name)

────────────────────
_ path-to [SyntaxId]
    - node SyntaxId

` The cases from the machine's root down to a case, the case last; a continuation that enters a
` case none writes is alone.
tree.path-to(machining.items, node)

────────────────────
_ do bind-path
    - node SyntaxId

` The names the activations of a case and of the cases above it see, bound from the root down,
` as the reference binds the path of the case.
for item in path-to(node)
    bind-activation(item)

────────────────────
_ do emit-entries
    - node SyntaxId

` The statements a case's or a continuation's body runs as it is entered, in order; a named
` machine among them starts there (`start-nested`).
for item in tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node))
    if tree.nested-machine(item) != 0
        start-nested(item)
    else if tree.is-entry-item(item)
        emit-statement(item)

────────────────────
_ do make-payload Typed
    - activation SyntaxId
    - type TypeId
    - position U32

` What a case holds, made of what a transition gives it: each value converted as the type
` pass recorded, alone or as the fields of a tuple. A case given nothing holds its number, as
` a union's case with no value of its own does.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
if type == types.void-type
    . union = layout-of(machining.fact!.union, activation)
    if !tables.layouts.is-union(union)
        refuse(.refused-expression, activation)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    = Typed(integer(.machine-u8, position), tables.layouts.case-field(union, position).type)
. targets = tree.state-targets(activation)
if targets.count == 1
    . target = tree.children[targets.start]
    . value = convert(target, .reason-argument, emit-expression(target))
    if value.type != type
        refuse(.refused-conversion, target)
    = value
. layout = layout-of(type, activation)
if !tables.layouts.is-struct(layout)
    refuse(.refused-expression, activation)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. made = frame(layout)
zero(made, layout)
. offset = 0u32
for target in tree.children[targets]
    . value = convert(target, .reason-argument, emit-expression(target))
    . field = tables.layouts.field(layout, offset)
    if value.type != field.type
        refuse(.refused-conversion, target)
        = Typed(nothing, no-type)
    put(made, field, value.operand, target)
    offset += 1
= Typed(made, type)

────────────────────
_ do store-machine
    - value Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` Keeps the machine's value: in its environment, and in the local, the global or the property
` that names it, or the name a named machine written in a case of another declares. A global
` holds a value from then on, so its state says so, and its cases read it as the reference's
` do while the machine starts. A machine that refines another keeps none: the cases it adds are
` none of the union the property holds.
if machining.fact!.refined != no-instance
    =
keep(machining.fact!.syntax, "(value)", value, site)
. named = machining.fact!.store == .store-nested && machining.slots!.bound != no-slot
if machining.fact!.store == .store-local || named
    keep-captured(machining.slots!.bound, value, machining.fact!.union, site)
else if machining.fact!.store == .store-member
    . name = decl-name(machining.fact!.module, machining.fact!.decl)
    if name
        put-member(name, value, site)
    else
        refuse(.refused-statement, site)
else if machining.fact!.store == .store-global
    . row = tables.storage-of(machining.fact!.module, machining.fact!.decl)
    if row == no-storage
        refuse(.refused-statement, site)
        =
    . kept = tables.storage[row]
    store-global(kept, value, site)
    if kept.state != no-string
        store-release(make-operand(.operand-symbol, kept.state), 0, integer(.machine-u8, 1), site)

────────────────────
_ do keep-active
    - held SyntaxId
    - active Bool
    - site SyntaxId

` Keeps whether the case kept at a node is active: in the machine's environment, and where a
` property of a class holds the machine or its markup writes it, in the object's flag of the
` case too, as the reference keeps it. A case of a machine of a class's markup that holds a
` value has no flag but its projection (`project`).
keep(held, "(active)", integer(.machine-u8, if active then 1 else 0), site)
if machining.fact!.store == .store-content && case-type(held) == types.void-type
    put-member(tree.state-name(held)!, integer(.machine-u8, if active then 1 else 0), site)
if machining.fact!.store != .store-member
    =
. name = decl-name(machining.fact!.module, machining.fact!.decl)
if !name
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    =
put-member
    - program.store-atom("(${name.text}-${tree.state-name(held)!.text}-active)")
    - integer(.machine-u8, if active then 1 else 0)
    - site

────────────────────
_ do put-member
    - name Atom
    - value Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` Stores a value in a stored property of the object a machine is written for, as an assignment
` does.
. found = property-of(unit.owner-type, name) if unit.has-self
. held = if found then tables.layouts.objects[unit.owner-type] else no-layout
if !found || held == no-layout || types.properties[found].storage-kind != .storage-eager
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    =
. property = types.properties[found]
put-property
    - unit.self
    - tables.layouts.field(held, object-header-fields + property.slot)
    - property
    - value
    - site
    - U32.max
    - false
    - memo-flag-of(unit.owner-type, property)

────────────────────
_ do keep-names
    - held SyntaxId
    - activation SyntaxId
    - position U32

` Keeps each name a case keeps from what entered it: what the name reads where the transition
` that enters it fires, or where none is in reach there, no object for a class or an interface,
` a named tuple or struct with its fields' first values, as the reference constructs one with
` no argument, and else the value a local of its type has with none written, as the reference
` keeps it. A named tuple or struct that declares a constructor has no shape here.
for name in machining.kept[position]
    . text = "(kept ${name.text})"
    . read = kept-read(activation, name)
    if read != no-slot
        . value = read-machine-name(read, activation)
        keep(held, text, value.operand, activation)
        continue
    . type = kept-type(held, text, activation)
    . layout = layout-of(type, activation)
    . value = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
    if tables.is-class(type) && (layout == pointer-layout || layout == managed-layout)
        value = integer(layout as MachineKind, 0)
    else if intrinsic(type) == .interface && tables.layouts.is-struct(layout)
        value = null-value(type, layout, activation).operand
    else if is-aggregate(type) && !types.is-plain-tuple(type)
        if tables.writes-constructor(type)
            refuse(.refused-type, activation)
            =
        value = make-fields(type, layout, RowRange'ArgumentFill(), given.length, 0, activation)
    else
        value = default-value(0, type, layout, activation).operand
    keep(held, text, value, activation)

────────────────────
_ do kept-read SlotId
    - activation SyntaxId
    - name Atom

` The local a name a case keeps reads where a transition enters the case, or none.
for read in bindings.machine-reads
    if read.module == machining.fact!.module && read.site == activation && read.name == name
        = read.slot
= no-slot

────────────────────
_ do read-machine-name Typed
    - slot SlotId
    - site SyntaxId

` What a name in reach where a transition fires holds: a name its pattern bound too.
. offset = slot-offset(slot, site)
if is-bound(slot)
    = read-bound(slot, site, facts.slot-type(unit.instance, offset))
if is-captured(slot)
    . held = find-captured(slot, site).type
    = read-captured(slot, site, held)
= read-local(slot, site, facts.slot-type(unit.instance, offset))

────────────────────
_ do add-one Operand
    - value Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` A generation after another.
= arithmetic(site, .arithmetic-add, value, integer(.machine-u32, 1), u32-layout)

────────────────────
_ do project
    - node SyntaxId
    - active Bool
    - payload Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` A case's projection, where the machine projects its cases: whether it is active, or what it
` holds while it is, and nothing while it is not. A machine of a class's markup projects what a
` case holds in the object's property of its name (`project-member`).
if machining.fact!.store == .store-content
    project-member(node, active, payload, site)
    =
if machining.fact!.store != .store-none
    =
. slot = bindings.declared-at(binding-slots(), machining.fact!.syntax, tree.state-name(node)!)
if slot == no-slot
    =
. held = find-captured(slot, site).type
if held == types.bool-type
    keep-captured(slot, integer(.machine-u8, if active then 1 else 0), held, site)
    =
. layout = layout-of(held, site)
. value = empty-optional(held, layout)
if active
    value = wrap(site, Typed(payload, types.optional-inner(held)), held)
keep-captured(slot, value.operand, held, site)

────────────────────
_ do project-member
    - node SyntaxId
    - active Bool
    - payload Operand
    - site SyntaxId

` What a case of a machine of a class's markup that holds a value holds while it is active, and
` nothing while it is not, in the object's property of its name, as the reference projects it.
if case-type(node) == types.void-type
    =
. name = tree.state-name(node)!
. found = property-of(unit.owner-type, name) if unit.has-self
if !found
    refuse(.refused-statement, site)
    =
. held = types.properties[found].type
. layout = layout-of(held, site)
. value = empty-optional(held, layout)
if active
    value = wrap(site, Typed(payload, types.optional-inner(held)), held)
put-member(name, value.operand, site)

────────────────────
_ do exit-case
    - node SyntaxId

` Exits a case, as the reference expands its exit: its active cases exit, last first; the
` activations of it and the cases above it are bound, its groups are unsubscribed, and those of
` each other continuation that enters it, it is no longer active nor projected so, and its
` `do finally` blocks run and the named machines written in it stop, last first, and then the
` tasks its activation owns are cancelled (`close-tasks`). The turns of the activations it binds
` end there. Where the machine is a piece of a composite, the cases below it are the composite's
` (`exit-below`), the pieces below this one that name the case again unsubscribe the groups they
` add after these, and run what they add to its exit before these, last first; one a piece above
` writes is exited by that piece.
if foreign-case(node)
    . case = composite-case(node)
    do call-part(machining.composite!.owners[case], case, .part-exit, node)
    =
. items = tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node))
exit-below(node)
. turns = open-turns.length
. rebound = rebindings.length
bind-path(node)
unsubscribe-groups(items)
for continuation in tree.continuations-named(machining.items, tree.state-name(node)!)
    if continuation != node
        unsubscribe-groups(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(continuation)))
contribute(node, .part-unsubscribe)
keep-active(case-node(node), false, node)
project(node, false, make-operand(.operand-void, 0), node)
contribute(node, .part-finally)
finish-items(items)
close-tasks(case-node(node), node)
close-turns(turns)
restore-cells(rebound)

────────────────────
_ do finish-items
    - items [SyntaxId]

` The `do finally` blocks of a body run and the named machines written in it stop, last first.
. place = items.length
while place != 0
    place -= 1
    if tree.nested-machine(items[place]) != 0
        stop-nested(items[place])
        continue
    match? tree.nodes[items[place]]
        | .node-do-finally-block(row)
            emit-block(row.body)

────────────────────
_ do exit-below
    - node SyntaxId

` Exits each active case written below a case, last first: those of the machine's composite,
` where it is a piece of one, each exited by the piece that writes it, those the pieces below
` this one write first (`relay-part`).
if !machining.composite
    . cases = tree.explicit-cases(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(node)))
    . position = cases.length
    while position != 0
        position -= 1
        exit-case-if-active(cases[position])
    =
. case = composite-case(node)
if below-adds(case, .part-exit-added)
    do call-below(case, .part-exit-added, nowhere(), nowhere(), node)
exit-composite(machining.composite!.descendants(case))

────────────────────
_ do exit-composite
    - cases [U32]

` Exits each active case of the machine's composite of those given, last first, by the piece
` that writes it.
. position = cases.length
while position != 0
    position -= 1
    . case = cases[position]
    . owner = machining.composite!.owners[case]
    if owner == machining.piece
        exit-case-if-active(machining.composite!.node(case, owner))
    else
        do call-part(owner, case, .part-exit, machining.fact!.syntax)

────────────────────
_ do exit-case-if-active ?! Refused
    - node SyntaxId

` Exits a case where it is active; one another piece of the machine's composite writes is exited
` by that piece.
if foreign-case(node)
    exit-case(node)
    =
. running = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
branch(read-flag(node, node).operand, running, done)
ir.start-block(running)
exit-case(node)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)

────────────────────
_ do exit-all

` Exits each active case of the machine, last first. Where the machine is a piece of a
` composite, the machine none refines exits each of the composite's, those the pieces below it
` write first (`relay-part`), and then those only a continuation enters.
if machining.composite && machining.piece != 0
    do call-part(0, U32.max, .part-exit-all, machining.fact!.syntax)
    =
. position = machining.cases.length
if machining.composite
    if below-adds(U32.max, .part-exit-added)
        do call-below(U32.max, .part-exit-added, nowhere(), nowhere(), machining.fact!.syntax)
    exit-composite(machining.composite!.descendants(U32.max))
while position != 0
    position -= 1
    if composite-case(machining.cases[position]) == U32.max
        exit-case-if-active(machining.cases[position])

────────────────────
_ do exit-descendants
    - node SyntaxId

` Exits each active case written in a case's body, last first; those of a case another piece of
` the machine's composite writes are exited by that piece.
if foreign-case(node)
    . case = composite-case(node)
    do call-part(machining.composite!.owners[case], case, .part-exit-below, node)
    =
exit-below(node)

────────────────────
_ do fire-event
    - transition SyntaxId
    - owner SyntaxId

` A transition a group's item passed, as the reference fires it from the case the group's owner
` names: a case exits the cases active below that case, or every active case at the root, and
` is entered; a continuation into a case written in the machine leaves the branch the two do not
` share (`move-between`), and any other exits that case, or every active case, and enters the
` case it names. One into a case another piece of the machine's composite writes, which this
` piece does not name, moves there by the composite's paths (`move-into`).
. found = if owner != 0 then tree.find-case(machining.items, tree.state-name(owner)!) else 0
. leaving = if found != 0 then found else owner
if tree.nodes[transition] is .node-state-case
    if leaving != 0
        exit-descendants(leaving)
    else
        exit-all()
    enter-case(transition, 0)
    =
. target = tree.find-case(machining.items, tree.state-name(transition)!)
. steps = composite-path(tree.state-name(transition)!)
if steps.length != 0
    move-into(leaving, steps, transition)
    =
if leaving != 0 && target != 0
    move-between(leaving, target, transition)
    =
if leaving != 0
    exit-case-if-active(leaving)
else
    exit-all()
enter-continuation(transition)

────────────────────
_ do move-between
    - source SyntaxId
    - target SyntaxId
    - via SyntaxId

` A continuation from a case into another case written in the machine, as the reference moves
` between them: the case on the source's path where the two paths part exits, and the cases of
` the target's path from there on are entered, the target by the continuation.
. depth = tree.transition-depth(machining.items, source, target)
exit-case-if-active(path-to(source)[depth])
enter-path(path-to(target), depth, via)

────────────────────
_ do move-into
    - source SyntaxId
    - steps [U32]
    - via SyntaxId

` A continuation from a case, or from the root for none, into a case of the machine's composite
` that this piece does not name, whose path `steps` is, as `move-between` moves: below the case
` where the case is on that path, its active cases exited, and else from where the two paths
` part, the case on the source's path there exited.
if source == 0
    exit-all()
    enter-steps(steps, 0, via)
    =
. leaving = path-to(source)
. origin = composite-steps(leaving)
if origin.length == 0
    refuse(.refused-statement, via)
    =
. place = steps.find(origin[origin.length - 1])
if place != null && place + 1 < steps.length
    exit-descendants(source)
    enter-steps(steps, place + 1, via)
    =
. depth = 0
while depth < origin.length && depth < steps.length && origin[depth] == steps[depth]
    depth += 1
if depth >= origin.length
    depth = origin.length - 1
if depth >= steps.length
    depth = steps.length - 1
exit-case-if-active(leaving[depth])
enter-steps(steps, depth, via)

────────────────────
_ do enter-continuation
    - continuation SyntaxId

` Enters the case a continuation names, its own entry statements first; one no case is written
` for is entered as that case, and one only another piece of the machine's composite writes is
` entered by that piece.
. target = tree.find-case(machining.items, tree.state-name(continuation)!)
. steps = composite-path(tree.state-name(continuation)!)
if steps.length != 0
    enter-steps(steps, steps.length - 1, continuation)
else if target == 0
    enter-case(continuation, 0)
else
    enter-case(target, continuation)

────────────────────
_ do fire-fallback
    - fallback SyntaxId

` A fallback where no transition of its group passed: the case it names exits where it is
` active, or one no case is written for is no longer active; one only another piece of the
` machine's composite writes is exited by that piece.
. target = tree.find-case(machining.items, tree.state-name(fallback)!)
. steps = composite-path(tree.state-name(fallback)!)
if steps.length != 0
    . case = steps[steps.length - 1]
    do call-part(machining.composite!.owners[case], case, .part-exit, fallback)
else if target != 0
    exit-case-if-active(target)
else
    keep-active(case-node(fallback), false, fallback)

────────────────────
_ do emit-immediates
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - active SyntaxId
    - settles Bool = false

` A body's immediate transitions, as the reference runs them once it is entered: each tests its
` condition, or matches its subject with its pattern, in turn, and a continuation with no trigger
` always passes; the first that passes leaves the case entered, `active`, or every active case
` where none was, as `pass-immediate` says, and enters its case, and where a part tries them,
` it answers so (`immediate-passed`). Where none passes, a case that `settles` enters its first
` case, and then their fallback fires. Where the machine is a piece of a composite, those the
` pieces below this one add to the case are tried after these, and the first case is the
` composite's (`settle-steps`). A first case given what its name is written with
` that the binder did not bind there (`enters-initial`) has no shape here.
. transitions = tree.immediate-transitions(items)
. initial = if settles then tree.initial-case(items) else 0
if initial != 0 && !tree.enters-initial(machining.items, active)
    refuse(.refused-statement, initial)
    =
. merged = settles && active != 0 && composite-case(active) != U32.max
. done = ir.reserve-block()
for transition in transitions
    . trigger = tree.state-trigger(transition)
    if trigger == 0
        pass-immediate(active, transition)
        note-passed(transition)
        jump(done)
        ir.start-block(done)
        =
    . next = ir.reserve-block()
    . subject = tree.trigger-subject(trigger)
    if subject != 0
        . value = emit-expression(subject)
        do emit-pattern(tree.trigger-match(trigger), value, next)
    else
        . condition = tree.trigger-condition(trigger)
        . passed = ir.reserve-block()
        branch-on(condition, passed, next)
        ir.start-block(passed)
    pass-immediate(active, transition)
    note-passed(transition)
    jump(done)
    ir.start-block(next)
if merged
    settle-steps(active, done)
else if initial != 0
    enter-case(initial, 0)
. fallback = tree.immediate-fallback(items)
if fallback != 0
    fire-fallback(fallback)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)

────────────────────
_ do note-passed
    - site SyntaxId

` Keeps that an immediate transition a part tried passed, where one does.
if immediate-passed != no-local
    store-local(immediate-passed, integer(.machine-u8, 1), site)

────────────────────
_ do settle-steps
    - active SyntaxId
    - done IRBlockId

` What settles a case this piece of the machine's composite writes where none of its own
` immediate transitions passed: those the pieces below it in the composite of the object's class
` add to it, tried by the part of the one below it (`relay-part`), one that passes leaving to
` `done`; then its first case of those every piece writes in it, this piece's where it writes
` one, else the first a piece below writes, entered by that piece.
. case = composite-case(active)
if below-adds(case, .part-immediates)
    . passed = call-below(case, .part-immediates, nowhere(), nowhere(), active)
    . next = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(compare(active, .compare-not-equal, passed.operand, integer(.machine-u8, 0)), done, next)
    ir.start-block(next)
. first = first-written(machining.composite!, machining.piece, case)
if first != U32.max
    enter-case(machining.composite!.node(first, machining.piece), 0)
else if below-adds(case, .part-initial)
    do call-below(case, .part-initial, nowhere(), nowhere(), active)

────────────────────
_ do pass-immediate
    - active SyntaxId
    - transition SyntaxId

` An immediate transition that passed where a case was entered, as the reference passes it: a
` continuation into a case written below that case enters the path down to it from there, its
` active cases exited; one into another case written in the machine leaves the branch the two do
` not share (`move-between`); a case written in the body of the case entered exits only that
` case's active cases. Anything else exits the case entered, or every active case where none
` was, and enters its case. A continuation into a case another piece of the machine's composite
` writes, which this piece does not name, moves there by the composite's paths (`move-into`).
. continuation = tree.nodes[transition] is .node-state-continuation
. target = if continuation then tree.find-case(machining.items, tree.state-name(transition)!) else 0
. steps = if continuation then composite-path(tree.state-name(transition)!) else List'U32()
if active != 0 && steps.length != 0
    move-into(active, steps, transition)
    =
if active != 0 && target != 0
    . path = path-to(target)
    . place = path.find(active)
    if place != null && place + 1 < path.length
        exit-descendants(active)
        enter-path(path, place + 1, transition)
        =
    move-between(active, target, transition)
    =
. children [SyntaxId]
if active != 0
    children = tree.child-cases(tree.state-items(tree.state-body(active)))
if !continuation && active != 0 && children.find(transition) != null
    exit-descendants(active)
    enter-case(transition, 0)
    =
if active != 0
    exit-case-if-active(active)
else
    exit-all()
if continuation
    enter-continuation(transition)
else
    enter-case(transition, 0)

────────────────────
_ do machine-group-of U32
    - head SyntaxId

` The place among the facts' groups of the group a transition heads, or none.
for position in machining.fact!.groups.start .. < machining.fact!.groups.start + machining.fact!.groups.count
    if facts.machine-groups[position].head == head
        = position
= U32.max

────────────────────
_ do subscribe-groups
    - items [SyntaxId]

` Subscribes each group of a body's event transitions, as the reference does: its stream is
` made a broadcaster, a record of the activation is made, which holds the machine's
` environment, says it is current and not yet subscribed, and the subscriber the activation's
` function runs with the record is kept with the broadcaster. The record is then subscribed,
` and the subscriber given to the broadcaster's `subscribe`, whose error is given to the global
` `unhandled-error`, with the group's deferral, which runs the activation through the event
` runtime's queue. A group on an event of an object attaches the port the machine keeps for it
` to the endpoint the event runtime keeps for the event (`attach-group`). One the event runtime
` runs from the table of the class is not subscribed: the object holds its port for the table.
` A group on a stream that is only iterable is read at once (`iterate-group`). One on an event
` that is not live (`settle-events`) evaluates only the object, as a loop on it does, and
` subscribes nothing.
for head in tree.group-heads(items)
    if joins-earlier(head)
        continue
    . place = machine-group-of(head)
    . record = tables.machine-record
    . handler = if place != U32.max then tables.machine-handler-of(place) else no-function
    if handler == no-function || record == no-layout || unit.environment == no-local
        refuse(.refused-statement, head)
        =
    . group = facts.machine-groups[place]
    . trigger = tree.group-trigger(head)
    if group.iterated
        iterate-group(head, group, handler)
        continue
    if group.lowered
        lower-group(head, place, handler)
        continue
    if group.event != U32.max
        . used = facts.event-uses[group.event]
        if tables.event-number(used.owner, used.name) == U32.max
            event-owner(used.reference, used.owner)
        else
            attach-group(head, group, handler)
        continue
    . stream = emit-broadcastable(trigger, tree.group-stream(head))
    . mark = pending.length
    pending += integer(.machine-u64, tables.layouts.rows[record].size)
    pending += make-operand(.operand-descriptor, record)
    . made = call-runtime(.runtime-allocate-object, head, mark, managed-layout)
    store(made, tables.layouts.field(record, 0).offset, load-local(unit.environment, head), true, head)
    store(made, tables.layouts.field(record, 1).offset, integer(.machine-u8, 1), false, head)
    . subscriber = make-callback(handler + 3, made, head)
    . subscribers = kept-type(head, "(subscriber)", head)
    . sources = kept-type(head, "(source)", head)
    keep(head, "(subscriber)", wrap(head, Typed(subscriber, group.subscriber), subscribers).operand, head)
    keep(head, "(source)", wrap(head, Typed(stream.operand, group.stream), sources).operand, head)
    store(made, tables.layouts.field(record, 2).offset, integer(.machine-u8, 1), false, head)
    call-subscription(head, group.subscribe, stream.operand, group.stream, subscriber, group.subscriber)

────────────────────
_ do attach-group
    - head SyntaxId
    - group MachineGroup
    - handler FunctionId

` Attaches the port the machine keeps for a group on an event of an object to the endpoint the
` event runtime keeps for the event, as the reference does where the group's owner enters: the
` port is made the first time, with the subscriber the group's activation runs with the
` machine's environment, and kept for the next time.
. stream = event-stream(tree.group-trigger(head), facts.event-uses[group.event])
. ports = kept-type(head, "(subscriber)", head)
. mark = pending.length
pending += read-kept(head, "(subscriber)", head).operand
pending += make-callback(handler + 2, load-local(unit.environment, head), head)
pending += stream.operand
. port = call-instance(group.attach, head, mark)
keep(head, "(subscriber)", wrap(head, port, ports).operand, head)

────────────────────
_ do iterate-group
    - head SyntaxId
    - group MachineGroup
    - handler FunctionId

` A group on a stream that is only iterable, where its owner subscribes it, as the reference
` loops over it: the container is evaluated once and begun, and each item it gives is given to
` the group's handler with the machine's environment and the container, in a loop that does
` not poll; a stream is told after that the loop has ended.
. trigger = tree.group-trigger(head)
. written = tree.group-stream(head)
. slot = loop-slots(trigger)
. kind = hold-container(trigger, written, slot)
if kind != group.stream
    refuse(.refused-statement, head)
    =
begin-items(trigger, written, slot, kind)
. root = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
jump(root)
ir.start-block(root)
. item = read-items(trigger, trigger, written, slot, kind, done)
if item.type != group.item
    refuse(.refused-statement, head)
    =
. mark = pending.length
pending += load-local(unit.environment, head)
pending += item.operand
pending += state(slot, trigger).operand
ir.depend(.callee-function, handler, may-panic-dependency)
do call(handler-symbol, head, mark, .callee-function, u8-layout, !in-landing)
    .. handler-symbol = make-operand(.operand-symbol, tables.functions[handler].symbol)
jump(root)
ir.start-block(done)
if facts.plan-of(unit.reading, trigger) == .plan-stream-loop
    end-stream(trigger)

────────────────────
_ do event-stream Typed
    - trigger SyntaxId
    - used EventUse

` The endpoint the event runtime keeps for the event of an object a group of a machine's event
` transitions is on, or the one at the address of a keyed event, which the receiver claims,
` made the group's `Broadcastable` as the type pass recorded at its trigger.
. owner = event-owner(used.reference, used.owner)
. number = tables.event-number(used.owner, used.name)
if number == U32.max
    refuse(.refused-statement, trigger)
if used.address != 0
    . endpoint = keyed-endpoint(used.site, used, owner.operand, number)
    = convert(trigger, .reason-argument, endpoint)
= event-endpoint(trigger, used.first, owner.operand, number)

────────────────────
_ do lower-group
    - head SyntaxId
    - place U32
    - handler FunctionId

` A group the event runtime runs from the table of the class the machine is written for, as the
` reference makes it where the group would be subscribed: the port of the group is made, with
` the subscriber the group's activation runs with the machine's environment and no
` broadcaster, kept, and held by the object where the table's function finds it (see
` `emit-machine-descriptor`).
. group = facts.machine-groups[place]
. name = context-name(head)
. found = property-of(unit.owner-type, name) if name && unit.has-self
. object = if found then tables.layouts.objects[unit.owner-type] else no-layout
if !found || object == no-layout
    refuse(.refused-statement, head)
    =
. ports = kept-type(head, "(subscriber)", head)
. broadcaster = null-value(group.stream, layout-of(group.stream, head), head)
. mark = pending.length
pending += make-callback(handler + 2, load-local(unit.environment, head), head)
pending += broadcaster.operand
. port = call-instance(group.port, head, mark)
keep(head, "(subscriber)", wrap(head, port, ports).operand, head)
. property = types.properties[found]
. field = tables.layouts.field(object, object-header-fields + property.slot)
store(unit.self, field.offset, num-cast(head, port.operand, managed-layout, pointer-layout), false, head)

────────────────────
_ do context-name Atom?
    - head SyntaxId

` The name of the property of an object that holds the record of the activation of a group of
` the machine's event transitions for the table of its class.
for decl in program.modules[machining.fact!.module].decls
    match? decl
        | .decl-property(row)
            if row.context == head
                = row.name
= null

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-descriptor

` The function the event runtime calls for a group of a machine's event transitions that it runs
` from the table of the class, given the object and what was published, as the reference
` compiles it: where the object holds the port of the group, what was published is posted to it.
. group = facts.machine-groups[function.place]
. head = group.head
. row = machine-descriptor-of(function.place, function.type)
unit = unit.source-module = machine-module-of(function.place)
ir.add-argument(managed-layout)
ir.add-argument(layout-of(group.item, head))
returns-type = types.void-type
ir.returns = void-layout
if !row || group.post == no-instance
    refuse(.refused-function, head)
    =
. name = context-name-in(unit.source-module, head)
. found = property-of(function.type, name) if name
. object = if found then tables.layouts.objects[function.type] else no-layout
if !found || object == no-layout
    refuse(.refused-function, head)
    =
. property = types.properties[found]
. field = tables.layouts.field(object, object-header-fields + property.slot)
. context = load(make-operand(.operand-argument, 0), field.offset, pointer-layout, head)
. posting = ir.reserve-block()
. done = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(head, .compare-not-equal, context, integer(.machine-pointer, 0)), posting, done)
ir.start-block(posting)
. mark = pending.length
pending += num-cast(head, context, pointer-layout, managed-layout)
pending += make-operand(.operand-argument, 1)
do call-instance(group.post, head, mark)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
return-nothing()

────────────────────
_ do machine-descriptor-of MachineDescriptor?
    - group U32
    - type TypeId

` The row of the functions the event runtime's table runs for a group of a machine's event
` transitions on an object of a class, or none.
for row in tables.machine-descriptors
    if row.group == group && row.type == type
        = row
= null

────────────────────
_ do machine-module-of ModuleId
    - group U32

` The module of the machine a group of event transitions is of.
for machine in facts.machines
    if group >= machine.groups.start && group < machine.groups.start + machine.groups.count
        = machine.module
= 0

────────────────────
_ do context-name-in Atom?
    - module ModuleId
    - head SyntaxId

` The name of the property that holds the record of the activation of a group of a machine's
` event transitions, among the declarations of the machine's module.
for decl in program.modules[module].decls
    match? decl
        | .decl-property(row)
            if row.context == head
                = row.name
= null

────────────────────
_ do unsubscribe-groups
    - items [SyntaxId]
    - leaves-tabled Bool = false

` Unsubscribes each group of a body's event transitions that is subscribed, as the reference
` does: the activation's record says it is no longer current, the subscriber is given to the
` broadcaster's `unsubscribe` where the record was subscribed, whose error is given to the
` global `unhandled-error`, and the machine keeps no subscriber for the group. The port of a
` group on an event of an object is detached from its endpoint, which drops what it queued, and
` kept for the next time; one the table runs has no shape here, unless `leaves-tabled`, where it
` is left to the table. One on a stream that is only iterable was never subscribed.
for head in tree.group-heads(items)
    if joins-earlier(head)
        continue
    . place = machine-group-of(head)
    . record = tables.machine-record
    if place == U32.max || record == no-layout
        refuse(.refused-statement, head)
        =
    . group = facts.machine-groups[place]
    if group.iterated
        continue
    if group.event != U32.max
        if group.detach == no-instance && leaves-tabled
            continue
        if group.detach == no-instance
            refuse(.refused-statement, head)
            =
        . mark = pending.length
        pending += read-kept(head, "(subscriber)", head).operand
        do call-instance(group.detach, head, mark)
        continue
    . held = read-kept(head, "(subscriber)", head)
    . optional = held.type
    . holding = present(head, held)
    . running = ir.reserve-block()
    . done = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(holding.operand, running, done)
    ir.start-block(running)
    . subscriber = payload(head, Typed(held.operand, optional))
    . data = load
        - subscriber.operand
        - tables.layouts.field(tables.layouts.function-layout, 1).offset
        - managed-layout
        - head
    store(data, tables.layouts.field(record, 1).offset, integer(.machine-u8, 0), false, head)
    . subscribed = load(data, tables.layouts.field(record, 2).offset, u8-layout, head)
    . calling = ir.reserve-block()
    . called = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(compare(head, .compare-not-equal, subscribed, integer(.machine-u8, 0)), calling, called)
    ir.start-block(calling)
    . source = read-kept(head, "(source)", head)
    . stream = payload(head, source)
    call-subscription
        - head
        - group.unsubscribe
        - stream.operand
        - group.stream
        - subscriber.operand
        - group.subscriber
    jump(called)
    ir.start-block(called)
    . layout = layout-of(optional, head)
    keep(head, "(subscriber)", empty-optional(optional, layout).operand, head)
    jump(done)
    ir.start-block(done)

────────────────────
+ do machine-of-union MachineFact?
    - union TypeId

` The state machine whose union a type is, or none.
for machine in facts.machines
    if machine.union == union
        = machine
= null

────────────────────
+ do start-refined
    - machine MachineFact

` Starts a machine that refines another, as the reference starts the two merged: each machine
` that refines another, from the one of the object's class up, keeps what it keeps for the
` object, and then the machine none refines starts, through the facts of the instance that types
` its value for the class that declares it.
. current MachineFact? = machine
while current
    . own-unit = unit
    . own-filling = filling
    unit = unit.source-module = current.module
    unit = unit.reading = instances.rows[current.instance].enclosing
    filling = filling.root = current.syntax
    do emit-expression(current.syntax)
    unit = own-unit
    filling = own-filling
    current = facts.machine-of(current.refined) if current.refined != no-instance

────────────────────
+ resolves-member Bool
    - id SyntaxId

` Whether a name alone resolves to a member of the object the function is emitted for.
|? binding == no-binding
    false
??
    bindings.resolution-of(binding, id).kind == .resolve-member

.. binding = instances.rows[unit.reading].binding

────────────────────
+ do flag-name Atom
    - property Atom
    - name Atom

` The name of the object's flag of a case of the machine a property of its class holds.
= program.store-atom("(${property.text}-${name.text}-active)")

────────────────────
+ do composite-classes [TypeId]
    - fact MachineFact
    - root MachineFact
    - owner TypeId

` The classes whose objects start a machine a property of a class holds (`leaf-classes`), where
` it is, or refines, the machine of a union, that are or derive from a class, or none.
. found [TypeId]
if fact.outer != 0
    = found
. top MachineFact? = fact
while top && top.refined != no-instance
    top = facts.machine-of(top.refined)
if !top || top.module != root.module || top.syntax != root.syntax
    = found
for type in tables.leaf-classes(fact)
    if derives(type, owner)
        found += type
= found

────────────────────
+ do classes-branch
    - site SyntaxId
    - value Operand
    - classes [TypeId]
    - matched IRBlockId
    - missed IRBlockId

` Leaves to `matched` when an object is of one of some classes itself, and to `missed` when it is
` of another.
. table = load(value, 0, pointer-layout, site)
for position in 0 .. < classes.length
    . next = if position + 1 == classes.length then missed else ir.reserve-block()
    . symbol = tables.table-symbols[classes[position]]
    if symbol == no-string
        jump(next)
    else
        branch
            - compare(site, .compare-equal, table, make-operand(.operand-symbol, symbol))
            - matched
            - next
    if position + 1 < classes.length
        ir.start-block(next)
if classes.length == 0
    jump(missed)

────────────────────
+ do derives Bool
    - type TypeId
    - base TypeId

` Whether a class is another or derives from it.
. level TypeId? = type
while level
    if level == base
        = true
    level = types.base-of(level)
= false

────────────────────
+ do emit-machine-path Typed
    - id SyntaxId
    - object SyntaxId

` `path` read from a value of a state machine's union, as the reference makes it: an empty list,
` given the name of each active case of the machine in turn, its cases written outermost first,
` each before those written in it, then those only a continuation enters. The flags are read
` where a case test reads them: those of a machine a property of a class holds from the object
` written before the property's name, evaluated once, or the one a name alone is read from; any
` other's as `machine-flag` reads them. Where the object is of a class whose composite merges the
` machine with refinements, the composite's cases are listed (`append-composite`). A value of the
` union read from elsewhere than the machine lists the case it holds after those it is written in,
` outermost first (`append-held`).
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. list-type = facts.node-type(unit.reading, id)
. union = facts.node-type(unit.reading, object)
. machine = machine-of-union(union)
. makes = no-fact
. append = no-instance
. fact = facts.first-call(unit.reading, id)
while fact != no-fact
    . row = facts.calls[fact]
    if row.form == .call-list-make
        makes = fact
    else if row.form == .call-method
        append = row.callee
    fact = row.next
if !machine || makes == no-fact || append == no-instance
    refuse(.refused-expression, id)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. member = machine.store == .store-member
. live = reads-machine(object, machine)
. base = nothing
. owner = no-type
. property = decl-name(machine.module, machine.decl)
if !live
    base = emit-expression(object).operand
else if member && property
    match? tree.nodes[object]
        | .node-get-expression(row)
            if row.name == property && !is-link(object)
                owner = held-type(row.object)
                base = emit-expression(row.object).operand
        | .node-identifier(row)
            if row.name == property && resolves-member(object)
                owner = self-owner()
                base = unit.self
    if owner == no-type || owner == invalid-type || !tables.is-class(owner)
        refuse(.refused-expression, object)
else if member || !(tree.nodes[object] is .node-identifier)
    refuse(.refused-expression, object)
. list = emit-fact-call(id, facts.calls[makes], 0, RowRange'SyntaxId(), 0, 0, list-type)
if list.type != list-type
    refuse(.refused-conversion, id)
. machine-tree = program.modules[machine.module].tree
. items = machine-tree.state-items(machine-tree.state-body(machine.syntax))
. cases = machine-tree.machine-cases(items)
. order [SyntaxId]
for node in machine-tree.explicit-cases(items)
    order += node
for node in cases
    if order.find(node) == null
        order += node
. done = ir.reserve-block()
if !live
    append-held(id, list.operand, append, base, machine, done)
    ir.start-block(done)
    = Typed(list.operand, list-type)
if member
    for position in tables.machine-order
        . fact = facts.machines[position]
        . classes = composite-classes(fact, machine, owner)
        . composite = compose-machine(program, facts, fact) if classes.length != 0
        if composite
            append-composite
                - id
                - list.operand
                - append
                - base
                - composite
                - property!
                - classes
                - tables.machine-receiver(fact)
                - done
for node in order
    . name = machine-tree.state-name(node)!
    . index = machine-tree.case-position(cases, name)!
    . flag = nothing
    if member
        . flagged = property-of(owner, flag-name(property, name)) if property
        if !flagged
            refuse(.refused-expression, id)
            = Typed(nothing, no-type)
        . field = held-field(id, owner, flagged)
        flag = load(base, field.offset, field.layout, id)
    else
        flag = machine-flag(id, machine, index, done).operand
    append-active(id, list.operand, append, flag, name)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(done)
= Typed(list.operand, list-type)

────────────────────
_ do append-active
    - id SyntaxId
    - list Operand
    - append InstanceId
    - flag Operand
    - name Atom

` Appends the name of a case to a machine's path where its flag says it is active.
. adding = ir.reserve-block()
. next = ir.reserve-block()
branch(compare(id, .compare-not-equal, flag, integer(.machine-u8, 0)), adding, next)
ir.start-block(adding)
append-name(id, list, append, name)
jump(next)
ir.start-block(next)

────────────────────
_ do append-name
    - id SyntaxId
    - list Operand
    - append InstanceId
    - name Atom

` Appends the name of a case to a machine's path.
. mark = pending.length
pending += list
pending += make-operand(.operand-constant, ir.add-string(name.text))
do call-instance(append, id, mark)

────────────────────
_ do append-held
    - id SyntaxId
    - list Operand
    - append InstanceId
    - value Operand
    - machine MachineFact
    - done IRBlockId

` Appends to a path read from a value of a state machine's union, read from elsewhere than the
` machine, the names of the case it holds, the innermost the machine was in when it was read, and
` of the cases that case is written in, outermost first, and leaves to `done`.
. machine-tree = program.modules[machine.module].tree
. items = machine-tree.state-items(machine-tree.state-body(machine.syntax))
. cases = machine-tree.machine-cases(items)
. tag = load(value, 0, u8-layout, id)
for position in 0 .. < cases.length
    . adding = ir.reserve-block()
    . next = ir.reserve-block()
    branch(compare(id, .compare-equal, tag, integer(.machine-u8, position as U64)), adding, next)
    ir.start-block(adding)
    for node in machine-tree.path-to(items, cases[position])
        append-name(id, list, append, machine-tree.state-name(node)!)
    jump(done)
    ir.start-block(next)
jump(done)

────────────────────
_ do append-composite
    - id SyntaxId
    - list Operand
    - append InstanceId
    - object Operand
    - composite MachineComposite
    - property Atom
    - classes [TypeId]
    - level TypeId
    - done IRBlockId

` Appends to a path, where an object is of one of the classes that run a composite typed for a
` class itself, the name of each active case of the composite, each before those written in it,
` then those only a continuation enters, and leaves to `done`.
. missed = ir.reserve-block()
. matched = ir.reserve-block()
classes-branch(id, object, classes, matched, missed)
ir.start-block(matched)
. names [Atom]
for name in composite.names
    names += name
for fact in composite.pieces
    . owner = program.modules[fact.module].tree
    for node in owner.machine-cases(owner.state-items(owner.state-body(fact.syntax)))
        if names.find(owner.state-name(node)!) == null
            names += owner.state-name(node)!
for name in names
    . flagged = property-of(level, flag-name(property, name))
    if !flagged
        refuse(.refused-expression, id)
        =
    . field = held-field(id, level, flagged)
    append-active(id, list, append, load(object, field.offset, field.layout, id), name)
jump(done)
ir.start-block(missed)

────────────────────
+ self-owner TypeId

` The class of the object a member's name alone is read from in the function being emitted, as
` `emit-identifier` reads it, or no type where it is read otherwise.
|? !unit.has-self
    no-type
|? unit.reading == unit.instance || unit.reading == unit.lender
    unit.owner-type
|? filling.count != 0
    no-type
|? unit.deferred-type != no-type
    unit.deferred-type
|? evaluates-value()
    unit.self-type
??
    no-type

────────────────────
+ do machine-default Typed
    - machine MachineFact
    - site SyntaxId

` What a property that holds a state machine holds until the machine starts: the first case of
` its union, as the reference gives a union no value is written for, holding what a local of its
` type holds with nothing written (`first-case`).
. layout = layout-of(machine.union, site)
if tables.layouts.is-union(layout)
    = first-case(machine.union, layout, site)
refuse(.refused-expression, site)
= Typed(make-operand(.operand-void, 0), no-type)

────────────────────
+ do machine-flag Typed
    - site SyntaxId
    - machine MachineFact
    - index U32
    - failed IRBlockId

` Whether a machine's case is active, where a case test is in reach of its flag: in the module
` of a machine a module's property is, from the global that holds its environment, which fails
` the test before the machine starts, in reach of the local a machine is kept in, beside it,
` and in the machine around a named machine written in a case of another. Elsewhere the case
` test is refused, as the reference tests the tag there.
. nothing = make-operand(.operand-void, 0)
. row = bindings.machine-slots(machine.module, machine.syntax)
. cases = program.modules[machine.module].tree.machine-cases
    - program.modules[machine.module].tree.state-items
        - program.modules[machine.module].tree.state-body(machine.syntax)
if !row || index >= cases.length as U32
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
. slot = bindings.machine-slot(row, cases[index], program.store-atom("(active)"))
if slot == no-slot
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
if machine.store == .store-local || (machine.store == .store-nested && machine.instance == unit.reading)
    = read-captured(slot, site, types.bool-type)
. storage = tables.storage-of(machine.module, instances.rows[machine.instance].decl)
. layout = tables.environments[machine.instance]
if machine.store != .store-global || storage == no-storage || foreign-machine || unbuilt-layout
    refuse(.refused-expression, site)
    = Typed(nothing, no-type)
.. foreign-machine = machine.module != instances.rows[unit.reading].module
.. unbuilt-layout = layout == no-layout || layout == unbuilt-environment
. field = tables.layouts.field(layout, 1 + tables.slot-fields[slot])
. base = load-global(tables.storage[storage], site)
pass-or-fail
    - compare(site, .compare-not-equal, base.operand, integer(managed-layout as MachineKind, 0))
    - failed
= Typed(load(base.operand, field.offset, field.layout, site), types.bool-type)
